<Layout title="College student medical care in Blacksburg | Kin & Campus" description="Ongoing medication follow-up, sick visits, asthma and allergy care, acne treatment, and university forms with a local board-certified pediatrician.">
<div class="w ph"><div class="eyebrow">Care</div><h1>Medical care that accounts for the way college students live.</h1><p class="lead">Students arrive in Blacksburg with established diagnoses, prescriptions, and routines that may be harder to maintain in a new setting. Kin &amp; Campus provides local follow-up and everyday medical care within a relationship that continues across the academic year.</p></div>
<div class="w"><img class="photo" src={href("photos/campus-aerial.jpg")} width="800" height="450" alt="Campus and the surrounding hills, seen from above">
<p class="lead" style="margin-top:36px">We begin with the student's history and current plan. From there, care can adapt thoughtfully as coursework, sleep, stress, seasons, and increasing independence affect their health.</p>
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row" id="adhd"><h3>ADHD medication</h3><p>For students with an established diagnosis, we review prior records, monitor treatment, and continue medication when clinically appropriate. Regular follow-up considers effectiveness, side effects, sleep, appetite, and the realities of the student's schedule.</p></div>
<div class="note-row" id="mental-health"><h3>Anxiety and depression medication</h3><p>We can follow established prescriptions, assess how treatment is working, and coordinate additional support when needed. Therapy and urgent mental health services are separate resources, and we help students understand when those services should be involved.</p></div>
<div class="note-row" id="asthma"><h3>Asthma and allergies</h3><p>We help students maintain controller and rescue plans, review triggers, and address changes in symptoms. Seasonal pollen, dorm environments, exercise, and dining changes can all affect management.</p></div>
<div class="note-row" id="acne"><h3>Acne</h3><p>Treatment is most useful when it is realistic enough to follow. We can adjust a plan over time and help students stay consistent despite changes in routine.</p></div>
<div class="note-row" id="illness"><h3>Common illnesses</h3><p>We evaluate concerns such as fever, sore throat, respiratory symptoms, and asthma flares, then recommend the appropriate next step based on the student's history and exam.</p></div>
<div class="note-row" id="forms"><h3>University and activity forms</h3><p>We review immunization, housing, sports, and travel paperwork and complete forms when the clinical information and requirements support it.</p></div>
</div></div>
<section><div class="w split"><svg class="art" viewBox="0 0 360 360" role="img" aria-label="Portrait placeholder"><rect width="360" height="360" rx="28" fill="#EADFCB"/><circle cx="180" cy="140" r="56" fill="#9CAF98"/><path d="M70 330q110-150 220 0z" fill="#6B2737"/><circle cx="270" cy="86" r="20" fill="none" stroke="#C9A24B" stroke-width="8"/></svg>
<div><div class="eyebrow">The physician</div><h2>A board-certified pediatrician based in Blacksburg.</h2><p class="lead">Young adults benefit from a physician who understands both adolescent medicine and the transition toward independent care. When a student's treatment changes, we communicate with the hometown physician when clinically appropriate and authorized. Emergency and after-hours needs should be directed to the appropriate emergency or urgent service.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">Care across the year</div><h2>Planned attention at useful moments.</h2>
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row"><h3>Move-in</h3><p>Establish care, review records and prescriptions, and address forms or practical questions before the semester is fully underway.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>During the semester</h3><p>Continue routine follow-up and respond to illness, changing symptoms, or treatment questions as they arise.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Breaks and finals</h3><p>Review medication supply, adherence, sleep, stress, and any issues that tend to surface when schedules change.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Year-end coordination</h3><p>Share clinically appropriate updates with the hometown physician so care can continue without unnecessary gaps.</p></div>
</div>
<p style="margin-top:36px"><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Discuss your student's needs</a></p></div></section>
</Layout>
